## Relationship Between Upper Systems and the Storage Layer

### Complete Call Relationship Diagram

```
InferenceInterceptor
        │
        ▼
CacheOrchestrator          ← The only runtime component that directly uses CacheStorage
   │    │    │
   │    │    └── write_async() → background thread → storage.batch_insert()
   │    │
   │    └── check(CP1/CP2/CP3)
   │              │
   │              ├── storage.search(QuerySpec) → list[SearchResult]
   │              │                                       │
   │              └── judge.evaluate(results)  ←──────────┘
   │                    reads result.payload.action_chunk
   │                    reads result.payload.intermediates
   │
   └── evict() → storage.delete(ids)

Offline tools (data pre-population)
        │
        └── storage.batch_insert(entries)   ← For cold-starting the cache
```

### SimilarityJudge Is Not a Storage Layer Component

The Judge's responsibility is: given `list[SearchResult]`, decide "hit or miss, full hit or warm start." It only cares about `result.score` and `result.payload` — independent of the backend.

The storage layer's responsibility ends when `search()` returns results. The Judge is an internal component of `CacheOrchestrator`, at the same level as `CacheStorage`, not subordinate to it.

This has a direct constraint on `SearchResult` design: **`SearchResult.payload` must be the strongly typed `CachePayload`**. Because the Judge needs `.action_chunk` and `.intermediates` — if it were a `dict`, there would be no type checking and errors would be easy. The serialization/deserialization logic (storing `CachePayload` into Qdrant payload and restoring from Qdrant payload) is fully encapsulated within the backend — the Judge is unaware of it.

### Summary of Each Layer's Responsibility Boundaries

| Layer | Component | Responsible For | Not Responsible For |
|-------|-----------|----------------|---------------------|
| Inference layer | `InferenceInterceptor` | Calling Orchestrator, handling cache hit/miss branches | Any storage details |
| Orchestration layer | `CacheOrchestrator` | Coordinating gate/search/judge/write flow | Knowing which DB is used |
| Orchestration layer | `SimilarityJudge` | Determining hit type, reading payload fields | Any storage details |
| Facade layer | `CacheStorage` | Combining backend + MetadataDB, exposing clean interface | DB internal implementation |
| Abstraction layer | `VectorStoreBackend` | Defining semantic contract (insert/search/delete/count) | Implementation details |
| Implementation layer | `QdrantVectorStore`, etc. | Serialization, network calls, score conversion | Business logic |

